# Uptime Kuma (`louislam-uptime-kuma`)

Experience seamless uptime monitoring with Uptime Kuma. This intuitive, self-hosted tool tracks diverse services and delivers rapid notifications to ensure your operations remain uninterrupted.

[Service documentation](https://docs.osaas.io/osaas.wiki/Service%3A-Uptime-Kuma.html) · [Source](https://github.com/louislam/uptime-kuma)

## Example

```terraform
resource "osc_instance" "example" {
  service_id = "louislam-uptime-kuma"
  name       = "mykuma"

  sensitive_parameters = {
    DatabaseUrl = var.database_url
  }
}
```

Commented lines are optional parameters. Values marked `"..."` need a real value. Outputs are `url`, `external_ip`, `external_port` and the raw `instance` document, see the `osc_instance` resource.

## Parameters

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `DatabaseUrl` | string | yes | Optional MariaDB connection URL in the form mysql://user:password@hostname:port/dbname (mariadb:// also accepted, port defaults to 3306). When set, the OSC wrapper writes it to Uptime Kuma's db-config.json as an external MariaDB; when empty, the built-in SQLite database in /app/data is used. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |

The instance `name` must match `^\w+$` and be unique per service within the workspace. OSC lowercases it and allows at most 20 characters.

Parameter values are strings; booleans take `"true"` or `"false"`. Reference an `osc_secret` as `osc_secret.<name>.ref` to keep a value out of the instance configuration. This page is generated from the OSC catalog; the provider validates against the live catalog when planning.
